      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9856]",
      "text": "The OSA design shall include all software necessary to support Target of Opportunity (ToO) observations during time allocated for both Pre-planned Queue Observing and Pi-Directed Observing Mode programs.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9856"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9333]",
      "text": "Each OSA software subsystem shall be built using the standard TMT software framework as provided by TMT Common Software and described in TMT Software Design Document (AD86), (AD87).",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9333"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9334]",
      "text": "Each OSA software subsystem shall be compliant with the TMT Software Development Process (AD79).",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9334"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9715]",
      "text": "All OSA software subsystems shall have the same CentOS 7 Linux deployment platform.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9715"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9953]",
      "text": "OSA software subsystems that require a private non-relational database or technical datastore shall integrate with the Observatory Databases through an HTTP-based interface.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9953"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9027]",
      "text": "OSA software subsystems shall use Graphical user interfaces (GUIs) as the default for all normal scientific and technical operations.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9027"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9029]",
      "text": "OSA software subsystems shall provide engineering GUIs if they include:\n� Low-level technical software parameter settings that are modifiable during operations.\n� Low-level engineering functions that are occasionally executed by an expert user.\n� Are required to operate in standalone mode.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9029"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9740]",
      "text": "The combined set of OSA software subsystems shall be implemented such that, without warning, they can be removed from the TMT operational environment then re-installed and restored to their operational state in less than eight (8) hours.",
      "id": "REQ-1-OAD-9740"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.2.1",
      "label": "[REQ-1-OAD-9000]",
      "text": "The OESA shall enable efficient observation of astronomical objects as well as efficient command, control, and monitoring of all observatory functions",
